window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-0462b3e291010c32"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"run-bulk-security-scans\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">运行批量安全扫描</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用 <code>npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan</code> 在一个扫描任务中检查多个代码仓库。你可以从个人 GitHub 账户或组织中发现代码仓库，也可以提供 CSV 文件，为每个代码仓库固定到一个确切的 Git 修订版本。</p> <p><code>@openai/codex-security</code> 软件包是公开发布的。执行扫描需要 Codex Security 访问权限。请按照 <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">CLI 快速入门</a>安装 CLI 并登录。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-repository-source\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择代码仓库来源</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>来源</th> <th>适用情形</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>GitHub 发现</td> <td>通过交互方式从个人 GitHub 账户或组织中选择代码仓库。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CSV 清单</td> <td>针对确切的代码仓库修订版本运行可重复、自动化的扫描任务。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>这两种流程都会保存进度、保留每个代码仓库的结果，并允许你在中断后继续扫描任务。</p> <p><a id=\"discover-github-repositories\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"github\">发现 GitHub 代码仓库</h2> <p>使用 GitHub CLI 登录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">gh auth login\n</code></pre> <p>开始交互式批量扫描：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan\n</code></pre> <p>CLI 会引导你完成以下步骤：</p> <ol> <li>选择个人 GitHub 账户或某个组织。</li> <li>查看最近 90 天内处于活跃状态的代码仓库。</li> <li>搜索代码仓库列表，并选择要扫描的仓库。</li> <li>选择扫描结果目录。</li> <li>检查所选仓库并确认扫描任务。</li> </ol> <p>扫描发现流程会排除已归档的代码仓库和 fork。CLI 会将每个已选仓库默认分支的确切提交版本记录到 <code>&lt;output-directory&gt;/repositories.csv</code>。在你确认所选仓库之前，不会开始扫描。</p> <p>若要使用 GitHub Enterprise Server，请先登录你的 GitHub 主机：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">gh auth login --hostname github.example.com\n</code></pre> <p>开始发现代码仓库时设置 <code>GH_HOST</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">GH_HOST=github.example.com npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan\n</code></pre> <p>交互式发现需要终端。若用于 CI、容器或预先准备好的仓库清单，请改用 CSV 清单。</p> <p><a id=\"create-a-repository-csv\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"csv\">创建代码仓库 CSV</h2> <p>创建 CSV 文件，每个代码仓库和固定修订版本占一行：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-csv\">id,repository,revision,scope,mode,prompt\npayments,https://github.com/example/payments.git,0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567,services/api,standard,Review payment authorization and refunds.\nidentity,https://github.com/example/identity.git,fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210fedcba98,,deep,Review session and identity boundaries.\n</code></pre> <p>CSV 支持以下列：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>列名</th> <th>必填</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>id</code></td> <td>是</td> <td>唯一的代码仓库标识符。可使用字母、数字、句点、连字符或下划线。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>repository</code></td> <td>是</td> <td>HTTPS URL、SSH URL 或本地代码仓库路径。相对路径以 CSV 所在目录为基准解析。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>revision</code></td> <td>是</td> <td>完整的 40 位或 64 位 Git 提交 SHA。当前不支持分支名称、标签和缩短的提交哈希。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>scope</code></td> <td>否</td> <td>相对于代码仓库根目录的扫描子目录。省略该值会扫描整个代码仓库。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>mode</code></td> <td>否</td> <td><code>standard</code> 或 <code>deep</code>。省略时使用命令选择的模式。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>prompt</code></td> <td>否</td> <td>针对该代码仓库的扫描说明。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>若要查找本地代码仓库的完整提交 SHA，请运行：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">git -C /path/to/repository rev-parse HEAD\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"run-a-campaign-from-csv\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"csv_1\">从 CSV 运行扫描任务</h2> <p>传入 CSV 文件以及一个位于各代码仓库之外的私密输出目录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4\n</code></pre> <p><code>--workers</code> 控制同时运行的代码仓库扫描数，默认值为 <code>4</code>。它不会设置每次深度扫描内部独立标准扫描工作进程的数量；请通过 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=configure-deep-scans\"><code>[deep_scan]</code></a> 配置这些限制。使用 <code>--mode\ndeep</code>，可以将 CSV 行中未单独指定 <code>mode</code> 的扫描设为深度扫描。每一行仍可自行选择扫描模式和代码仓库范围。</p> <p>设置 <code>[deep_scan].max_time_hours</code>，可以限制该扫描任务中每次深度扫描的工作进程运行时间。<code>--max-time-hours</code> 标志适用于 <code>scan</code>，不适用于 <code>bulk-scan</code>。</p> <p>CLI 会检出每个固定修订版本、扫描所选目标、记录结果，然后移除临时代码仓库检出目录。当某个代码仓库的扫描清单状态为 <code>completed</code>，且所需结果产物有效时，该仓库才算完成。覆盖缺口不会导致扫描失败。</p> <p><a id=\"share-security-context-and-instructions\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">分享安全上下文和指令</h2> <p>使用 <code>--knowledge-base</code>，可将架构文档、威胁模型或安全策略加入每次扫描。可以重复指定该标志，加入多个文件或目录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --knowledge-base /path/to/architecture.md \\\n  --knowledge-base /path/to/security-policies\n</code></pre> <p>若要加入共用的扫描指令，或在每次扫描后运行后续提示，请提供提示文件：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --scan-prompt-file scan-instructions.md \\\n  --post-scan-prompt-file follow-up.md\n</code></pre> <p>CLI 会在共用扫描指令之后追加 CSV 中每个代码仓库的 <code>prompt</code>。成功扫描和扫描错误后，后续指令会在同一已验证身份的会话中运行；取消扫描或达到费用上限后则不会运行。提示文件路径相对于当前目录解析。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-model-and-reasoning-effort\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">选择模型和推理强度</h2> <p>批量扫描默认使用 <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code> 模型和 <code>xhigh</code> 推理强度。若要为 CSV 扫描任务选择其他模型和强度，请确保你的凭据有权访问该模型。如果使用 ChatGPT 登录，请先查看 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol 的可用性</a>，再使用以下示例：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4 \\\n  --model gpt-6.1-sol \\\n  --effort medium\n</code></pre> <p>交互式发现代码仓库时也可以使用相同选项：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan --model gpt-6.1-sol --effort medium\n</code></pre> <p>不同模型支持的推理强度各不相同。批量扫描支持 <code>minimal</code>、<code>low</code>、<code>medium</code>、<code>high</code>、<code>xhigh</code> 和 <code>max</code>；GPT-6.1 Sol 至少需要 <code>low</code>。</p> <p>若要使用 OpenRouter 或 Fireworks，请分别设置 <code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code> 或 <code>FIREWORKS_API_KEY</code>，并指定 <code>--provider</code> 和 <code>--model</code>。凭据和示例请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=use-openrouter-or-fireworks\">OpenRouter 或 Fireworks 设置</a>或 <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=use-amazon-bedrock\">Amazon Bedrock 设置</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"review-campaign-results\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">查看扫描任务结果</h2> <p>输出目录会保存扫描任务配置、每次尝试的记录，以及每个代码仓库各自的结果：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">security-scans/\n├── manifest.json\n├── results.jsonl\n├── checkouts/\n└── artifacts/\n    ├── payments/\n    │   └── attempt-1/\n    │       ├── scan-manifest.json\n    │       ├── findings.json\n    │       ├── coverage.json\n    │       └── report.md\n    └── identity/\n        └── attempt-1/\n            ├── scan-manifest.json\n            ├── findings.json\n            ├── coverage.json\n            └── report.md\n</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>manifest.json</code> 记录该扫描任务中的代码仓库、固定修订版本、扫描范围、扫描模式，以及共用或针对单个仓库的指令。</li> <li><code>results.jsonl</code> 记录每次代码仓库扫描尝试的状态、产物目录，以及可用的费用或错误详情。</li> <li><code>report.md</code> 为某次代码仓库扫描尝试提供易读的报告。</li> <li><code>findings.json</code> 和 <code>coverage.json</code> 记录该次扫描尝试发现的问题和检查范围。</li> </ul> <p>若要导出某个已完成的代码仓库扫描，以便携带或分享：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security export \\\n  /path/outside/repositories/security-scans/artifacts/payments/attempt-1 \\\n  --export-format sarif \\\n  --output /path/outside/repositories/payments.sarif\n</code></pre> <p>结果可能包含源代码摘录和漏洞详情。请将输出目录保存在私密位置，并放在被扫描的代码仓库之外。设置结果保留时间。</p> <p><a id=\"resume-a-campaign\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">继续扫描任务</h2> <p>使用相同的 CSV 文件和输出目录再次运行原命令：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4\n</code></pre> <p>CLI 会继续扫描任务：为符合条件但尚未完成的仓库开始新的尝试，并跳过已完成的扫描，包括存在覆盖缺口的已完成扫描。之前的结果会保留供你查看。</p> <p>对于现有输出目录，不要更改代码仓库清单、扫描指令或后续指令。CLI 会检查固定的清单，并拒绝不同的扫描任务。如果更改了仓库、修订版本、扫描范围、扫描模式、共用指令或针对特定仓库的指令，请使用新的输出目录。</p> <p><a id=\"retry-repository-errors\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">重试代码仓库错误</h2> <p>使用 <code>--max-attempts</code>，在临时检出或扫描错误后重试该代码仓库：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4 \\\n  --max-attempts 3\n</code></pre> <p>默认情况下，每个代码仓库只尝试一次。每次尝试都有独立的结果记录和产物目录。重试适用于检出错误、扫描失败，以及必要产物缺失或无效等情况。不会因为覆盖缺口或严重级别策略违规而重试已完成的扫描。</p> <p>批量扫描使用以下退出码：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>退出码</th> <th>含义</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>0</code></td> <td>所有代码仓库均已完成，并且通过了任何已配置的严重级别策略。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>1</code></td> <td>扫描已完成，但发现项达到已配置的严重级别阈值。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>2</code></td> <td>某个代码仓库因输入、执行、结果完整性或必要输出错误而失败。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>130</code></td> <td>按下 Ctrl-C，中断了扫描任务。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>143</code></td> <td>SIGTERM 终止了扫描任务。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"run-bulk-scans-in-docker\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"docker\">在 Docker 中运行批量扫描</h2> <p><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security 代码仓库（需联网）</a>提供了经过加固的 Compose 配置，可在 Linux Docker 主机上自动运行 CSV 扫描任务。主机必须支持创建非特权用户命名空间。</p> <p>请将代码仓库 CSV、扫描结果和登录状态挂载到持久目录中。通过环境变量或密钥管理器提供 OpenAI 凭据。对于私有 GitHub 仓库，也要以相同方式提供 <code>GH_TOKEN</code> 或 <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code>。</p> <p>使用挂载的 CSV 和输出目录运行镜像：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">docker compose run --rm codex-security \\\n  bulk-scan /input/repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /output \\\n  --workers 4\n</code></pre> <p>继续扫描任务时，使用相同的挂载 CSV 和输出目录。对于 GitHub Enterprise Server，请将 <code>CODEX_SECURITY_GIT_HOST</code> 设为你的 GitHub 主机。</p> <p>所有可用标志请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-bulk-scan\">批量扫描命令参考</a>。有关扫描覆盖和发现项的常见问题，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-d4672d2ba61dcd68\">CLI 常见问题</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"run-bulk-security-scans\">Run bulk security scans</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan</code> to review repositories in one campaign. Discover repositories from your personal GitHub account or an organization, or provide a CSV that pins every repository to an exact Git revision.</p> <p>The <code>@openai/codex-security</code> package is public. Running scans requires Codex Security access. Follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">CLI quickstart</a> to install the CLI and sign in.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-repository-source\">Choose a repository source</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Source</th> <th>When to use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>GitHub discovery</td> <td>Choose repositories interactively from your personal GitHub account or an organization.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CSV inventory</td> <td>Run a repeatable, automated campaign against exact repository revisions.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Both workflows save progress, preserve per-repository results, and let you resume a campaign after an interruption.</p> <h2 id=\"discover-github-repositories\">Discover GitHub repositories</h2> <p>Sign in with GitHub CLI:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">gh auth login\n</code></pre> <p>Start an interactive bulk scan:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan\n</code></pre> <p>The CLI guides you through these steps:</p> <ol> <li>Choose your personal GitHub account or an organization.</li> <li>Review repositories active within the last 90 days.</li> <li>Search the repository list and select repositories to scan.</li> <li>Choose a directory for scan results.</li> <li>Review the selected repositories and confirm the campaign.</li> </ol> <p>Discovery excludes archived repositories and forks. The CLI records the exact default-branch commit for each selected repository in <code>&lt;output-directory&gt;/repositories.csv</code>. No scans start until you confirm the selection.</p> <p>To use GitHub Enterprise Server, first sign in to your GitHub host:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">gh auth login --hostname github.example.com\n</code></pre> <p>Set <code>GH_HOST</code> when you start repository discovery:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">GH_HOST=github.example.com npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan\n</code></pre> <p>Interactive discovery requires a terminal. For CI, containers, or a prepared repository list, use a CSV inventory instead.</p> <h2 id=\"create-a-repository-csv\">Create a repository CSV</h2> <p>Create a CSV with one row for each repository and pinned revision:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-csv\">id,repository,revision,scope,mode,prompt\npayments,https://github.com/example/payments.git,0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567,services/api,standard,Review payment authorization and refunds.\nidentity,https://github.com/example/identity.git,fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210fedcba98,,deep,Review session and identity boundaries.\n</code></pre> <p>The CSV supports these columns:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Column</th> <th>Required</th> <th>Description</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>id</code></td> <td>Yes</td> <td>Unique repository identifier. Use letters, numbers, periods, hyphens, or underscores.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>repository</code></td> <td>Yes</td> <td>HTTPS URL, SSH URL, or local repository path. Relative paths resolve from the CSV directory.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>revision</code></td> <td>Yes</td> <td>Full 40- or 64-character Git commit SHA. Branch names, tags, and shortened commit hashes aren't supported.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>scope</code></td> <td>No</td> <td>A repository-relative directory to scan. Omit the value to scan the full repository.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>mode</code></td> <td>No</td> <td><code>standard</code> or <code>deep</code>. Omit the value to use the command's selected mode.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>prompt</code></td> <td>No</td> <td>Scan instructions specific to this repository.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>To find a local repository's full commit SHA, run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">git -C /path/to/repository rev-parse HEAD\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"run-a-campaign-from-csv\">Run a campaign from CSV</h2> <p>Pass the CSV and a private output directory outside the repositories:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4\n</code></pre> <p><code>--workers</code> controls concurrent repository scans and defaults to <code>4</code>. It does not set the number of independent standard-scan workers within each deep scan; configure those limits through <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=configure-deep-scans\"><code>[deep_scan]</code></a>. Use <code>--mode\ndeep</code> to select deep scanning for rows without their own <code>mode</code>. Each CSV row can still choose its own scan mode and repository scope.</p> <p>Set <code>[deep_scan].max_time_hours</code> to limit worker execution for each deep scan in the campaign. The <code>--max-time-hours</code> flag works with <code>scan</code>, not <code>bulk-scan</code>.</p> <p>The CLI checks out each pinned revision, scans the selected target, records the result, and removes the temporary repository checkout. A repository counts as complete when its scan has a <code>completed</code> manifest status and valid required result artifacts. Coverage gaps don't make the scan fail.</p> <h2 id=\"share-security-context-and-instructions\">Share security context and instructions</h2> <p>Add architecture documents, threat models, or security policies to every scan with <code>--knowledge-base</code>. Repeat the flag for more files or directories:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --knowledge-base /path/to/architecture.md \\\n  --knowledge-base /path/to/security-policies\n</code></pre> <p>To add shared scan instructions or run a follow-up after each scan, provide prompt files:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --scan-prompt-file scan-instructions.md \\\n  --post-scan-prompt-file follow-up.md\n</code></pre> <p>The CLI appends each repository's CSV <code>prompt</code> after the shared scan instructions. Follow-up instructions run in the same authenticated session after successful scans and scan errors, but not after cancellation or a scan that reaches its cost limit. Prompt file paths resolve from your current directory.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-model-and-reasoning-effort\">Choose a model and reasoning effort</h2> <p>Bulk scans use <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code> with <code>xhigh</code> reasoning effort by default. To choose another model and effort for a CSV campaign, use a model your credentials can access. If you use ChatGPT sign-in, check <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol availability</a> before using this example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4 \\\n  --model gpt-6.1-sol \\\n  --effort medium\n</code></pre> <p>The same options work during interactive repository discovery:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan --model gpt-6.1-sol --effort medium\n</code></pre> <p>Available effort levels depend on the selected model. Bulk scans support <code>minimal</code>, <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code>, <code>high</code>, <code>xhigh</code>, and <code>max</code>; GPT-6.1 Sol requires at least <code>low</code>.</p> <p>To use OpenRouter or Fireworks, set <code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code> or <code>FIREWORKS_API_KEY</code>, respectively, and specify <code>--provider</code> and <code>--model</code>. For credentials and examples, see <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=use-openrouter-or-fireworks\">OpenRouter or Fireworks setup</a> or <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=use-amazon-bedrock\">Amazon Bedrock setup</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"review-campaign-results\">Review campaign results</h2> <p>The output directory keeps the campaign configuration, a record of each attempt, and separate results for each repository:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">security-scans/\n├── manifest.json\n├── results.jsonl\n├── checkouts/\n└── artifacts/\n    ├── payments/\n    │   └── attempt-1/\n    │       ├── scan-manifest.json\n    │       ├── findings.json\n    │       ├── coverage.json\n    │       └── report.md\n    └── identity/\n        └── attempt-1/\n            ├── scan-manifest.json\n            ├── findings.json\n            ├── coverage.json\n            └── report.md\n</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>manifest.json</code> records the repositories, pinned revisions, scopes, scan modes, and shared or repository-specific instructions in the campaign.</li> <li><code>results.jsonl</code> records each repository attempt, its status, artifact directory, and any available cost or error details.</li> <li><code>report.md</code> provides a readable report for one repository attempt.</li> <li><code>findings.json</code> and <code>coverage.json</code> record that attempt's findings and reviewed scope.</li> </ul> <p>Export one completed repository scan when you need a portable result:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security export \\\n  /path/outside/repositories/security-scans/artifacts/payments/attempt-1 \\\n  --export-format sarif \\\n  --output /path/outside/repositories/payments.sarif\n</code></pre> <p>Results can contain source excerpts and vulnerability details. Keep the output directory private and outside scanned repositories. Set how long to keep the results.</p> <h2 id=\"resume-a-campaign\">Resume a campaign</h2> <p>Run the original command with the same CSV and output directory:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4\n</code></pre> <p>The CLI resumes the campaign, starting new attempts for eligible unfinished repositories and skipping completed scans, including scans with coverage gaps. Their results remain available.</p> <p>Don't change the repository inventory or scan and follow-up instructions for an existing output directory. The CLI checks the pinned manifest and rejects a different campaign. Use a new output directory when you change repositories, revisions, scopes, scan modes, or shared or repository-specific instructions.</p> <h2 id=\"retry-repository-errors\">Retry repository errors</h2> <p>Use <code>--max-attempts</code> to retry a repository after a temporary checkout or scan error:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 4 \\\n  --max-attempts 3\n</code></pre> <p>The default is one attempt per repository. Each attempt has its own result record and artifact directory. Retries cover checkout errors, scan failures, and missing or invalid required artifacts. Completed scans aren't retried because of coverage gaps or severity-policy violations.</p> <p>Bulk scans use these exit codes:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Exit code</th> <th>Meaning</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>0</code></td> <td>Every repository completed, and any configured severity policy passed.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>1</code></td> <td>Scans completed, but findings met a configured severity threshold.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>2</code></td> <td>A repository failed because of an input, execution, result-integrity, or required-output error.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>130</code></td> <td>Ctrl-C interrupted the campaign.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>143</code></td> <td>SIGTERM terminated the campaign.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"run-bulk-scans-in-docker\">Run bulk scans in Docker</h2> <p>The <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security repository (online)</a> includes a hardened Compose configuration for automated CSV campaigns on a Linux Docker host. The host must support unprivileged user namespace creation.</p> <p>Keep the repository CSV, scan results, and sign-in state mounted in persistent directories. Supply OpenAI credentials through the environment or a secret manager. For private GitHub repositories, provide <code>GH_TOKEN</code> or <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> the same way.</p> <p>Run the image with the mounted CSV and output directory:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">docker compose run --rm codex-security \\\n  bulk-scan /input/repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /output \\\n  --workers 4\n</code></pre> <p>Use the same mounted CSV and output directory to resume the campaign. For GitHub Enterprise Server, set <code>CODEX_SECURITY_GIT_HOST</code> to your GitHub host.</p> <p>For every available flag, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-bulk-scan\">bulk-scan command reference</a>. For common questions about scan coverage and findings, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-d4672d2ba61dcd68\">CLI FAQ</a>.</p>"};
